      },
      "worked": "The square root must be real:\n$$\\begin{align*}2-x&\\geq0\\\\x&\\leq2\\end{align*}$$\nThe logarithm argument must be positive:\n$$\\begin{align*}1-\\sqrt{2-x}&>0\\\\\\sqrt{2-x}&<1\\\\2-x&<1\\\\x&>1\\end{align*}$$\nCombining the restrictions gives $D=(1,2]$. On this domain, $0<1-\\sqrt{2-x}\\leq1$. The argument equals $1$ at $x=2$ and approaches $0$ as $x\\to1^+$. Therefore $f(2)=0$ and $f(x)\\to-\\infty$ as $x\\to1^+$, so $R=(-\\infty,0]$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
